+---
+id: dl-005-createpatch-minimal-recursive-diff-index-wise-arrays
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch: minimal recursive diff, index-wise arrays"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two JSON versions, as a JSON Patch.
+
+## Decision
+
+Recursive diff: objects member by member (in `Object.keys` order, so output is deterministic), arrays
+index by index, anything else replaced. Array tail removals are emitted from the end. Values in the patch
+are cloned. `undefined` raises a TypeError, as in the other functions. No move/copy/test operations.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Patches are small for localized changes. An insertion at the front of a long array yields many operations
+rather than one `add`, since there is no LCS matching; this keeps the algorithm simple and predictable and
+can be refined later without changing the API.
